  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Schrödinger’s drug discovery segment shows strong momentum with surging collaboration-related revenue, while its core software business faces headwinds from a strategic move toward hosted and licensing-based models. The shift toward recurring, predictable revenue streams is still in transition, causing near-term software revenue volatility and contributing to a Q4 decline despite solid annual growth. Broader demand for AI-driven computational chemistry tools remains intact, but market sentiment has turned cautious, reflected in analyst target resets and persistent share-price weakness that highlights uncertainty around the software model’s adoption curve.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is accelerating a deliberate pivot to a licensing and subscription-oriented model to enhance revenue visibility, demonstrating conviction in long-term transformation over near-term linearity. Analysts have responded by trimming valuation estimates, signaling concern about execution risk, the pace of hosted software uptake, and the path to profitability. The company continues to reduce net losses and advance its AI platform capabilities, but the market’s confidence is strained by the stock’s significant multi-year decline and uncertainty about when the model transition will generate consistent growth. No capital-return initiatives are present, with focus squarely on reinvestment.",
